-- title:
--   Unit germs at the crossing point arise from unit sections
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero modulus $M$ with a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, together with $hpM : p \mid M$ and $hpM2 : p^2 \nmid M$; the hypothesis $hHp$ requires that every unit of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ whose image under the reduction map `ZMod.unitsMap` to $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$ lies in $H$ (so the kernel of reduction modulo $M/p$ is contained in $H$), and $M/p$ is nonzero. The hypothesis $hj$ asks that the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` lie in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the level-one integral form ratios. Finally $\mathfrak{X}$ is a model package `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`: this bundles a proper, flat, integral model `X p (ΓM M H) hj` over the coefficient ring $R_p$ with normal affine sections, a proper smooth model at the auxiliary level `ΓN p M H hpM`, a curve model `Meta` of the geometric function field `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with an isomorphism `eeta` of `Meta.C` onto the base change of the model to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ compatible with the structure morphisms, the Galois equivariance `hgal`, the pinning `Meta_pin` of the finite chart, and smoothness and geometric integrality of the generic fibre, among further clauses (summarised here).
--
--   Coefficient data. $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $hA$ asserting `A.LiesOverPrime p`, i.e. $p$ is a non-unit of $A$; the residue field of $A$ has characteristic $p$ and is algebraically closed. A ring map $\rho : R_p \to A$ is given with $h\rho$ saying that $\rho$ followed by the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the structure map $R_p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Next, $O$ is a discrete valuation domain with a map $\rho_O : R_p \to O$, with $h\varpi$ requiring that the maximal ideal of $O$ be generated by $p$; $to\kappa : O \to \mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$ satisfies $to\kappa \circ \rho_O = \mathrm{residue} \circ \rho$; $jO : O \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfies $jO \circ \rho_O =$ the structure map of $R_p$; and $\iota_A : O \to A$ satisfies $A.\mathrm{subtype} \circ \iota_A = jO$ and $\mathrm{residue} \circ \iota_A = to\kappa$.
--
--   The crossing point and its chart over $O$. Write `fibre` for the fibre of the model over the residue field of $A$ and, for $i = 0, 1$, let `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ i` be the two morphisms into it provided by the package; $n$ is a point of the fibre product of these two morphisms. Its image along `pullback.fst` followed by `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` followed by `bcMap (ΓM M H) hj ρO toκ htoκ` is a point $x_n$ of $X_O :=$ `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO`, the base change of the model along $\rho_O$. There are given an integer $e \ge 1$, an open $U$ of $X_O$ with $hxU : x_n \in U$, and a morphism $f$ from $U$ to `CrossingQuotient.crossingScheme ((p : O)^e)`, the spectrum of $Q := O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1 - p^e)$, subject to: $hover$, that $f$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $O \to Q$ equals the inclusion $U \hookrightarrow X_O$ followed by the structure morphism $X_O \to \operatorname{Spec} O$; $hfib$, that for $y \in U$ the two elements `CrossingQuotient.U ((p : O)^e)` and `CrossingQuotient.V ((p : O)^e)` of $Q$ both lie in the prime $f(y)$ if and only if the image of $y$ in $X_O$ is $x_n$; $hpt$, that for every $y \in U$ over $x_n$ the stalk map of $f$ at $y$ is flat, carries the maximal ideal onto the maximal ideal, and induces an isomorphism of residue fields; $het$, that every such $y$ has an open neighbourhood $V \subseteq U$ with $V \hookrightarrow U$ followed by $f$ étale; and the four conditions $hor_1$–$hor_4$, which say that for $y \in U$ one has `CrossingQuotient.V ((p : O)^e)` $\in f(y)$ exactly when the image of $y$ lies in the range of `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` followed by `bcMap (ΓM M H) hj ρO toκ htoκ` ($hor_1$ and $hor_3$), and `CrossingQuotient.U ((p : O)^e)` $\in f(y)$ exactly when that image lies in the range of the corresponding composite for the index $1$ ($hor_2$ and $hor_4$).
--
--   A second coefficient ring. $O'$ is a discrete valuation domain with maps $\sigma : O \to O'$ and $\iota_{A'} : O' \to A$ such that $\iota_{A'} \circ \sigma = \iota_A$, with $\iota_{A'}$ injective and local; $jO' : O' \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfies $jO' \circ (\sigma \circ \rho_O) =$ the structure map of $R_p$ and $A.\mathrm{subtype} \circ \iota_{A'} = jO'$; and $h to\kappa'$ records that $(\mathrm{residue} \circ \iota_{A'}) \circ (\sigma \circ \rho_O) = \mathrm{residue} \circ \rho$.
--
--   Notation introduced in the statement. $XQ$ is the base change of the model to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and $prJ : XQ \to X_O$, $prJ' : XQ \to X_{O'} :=$ `XO (ΓM M H) hj (σ.comp ρO)`, $pr\sigma : X_{O'} \to X_O$ and $prA : XQ \to X_A :=$ `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρ` are the maps of base changes induced by $jO$, $jO'$, $\sigma$ and $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; $VM$ is the open $\mathtt{eeta}^{-1}(prJ^{-1}(U))$ of `Meta.C`. With $\varphi : Q \to \Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} Q, \top)$ the inverse of `Scheme.ΓSpecIso`, the sections $gv$ and $gu$ of the structure sheaf of $X_O$ over the image open `U.ι ''ᵁ ⊤` are obtained by pulling the global sections corresponding to `CrossingQuotient.V ((p : O)^e)` and `CrossingQuotient.U ((p : O)^e)` back along $f$ and transporting along the isomorphism $\Gamma(X_O, U.\iota\,''\top) \cong \Gamma(U, \top)$. Given a hypothesis $hgen$ that the generic point of `Meta.C` lies in $\mathtt{eeta}^{-1}(prJ^{-1}(U.\iota\,''\top))$, the reading map $\mathrm{read} : \Gamma(X_O, U.\iota\,''\top) \to$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` is restriction along $prJ$, then along `eeta`, then the germ at the generic point of `Meta.C`, followed by the inverse of `Meta.ffEquiv`; and $\mathrm{param} := \mathrm{read}\, gv$. Further, $bc'$ denotes `bcMap (ΓM M H) hj (σ.comp ρO) ((residue A).comp ιA') htoκ'`, $x_n'$ the image of $n$ in $X_{O'}$ along `pullback.fst` followed by `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` followed by $bc'$, $B$ the stalk of $X_{O'}$ at $x_n'$, and $\sigma_B : O' \to B$ the germ at $x_n'$ of the structure map of $X_{O'}$ over $\operatorname{Spec} O'$. Given a hypothesis $hsp$ that the image of the generic point of `Meta.C` under `eeta` followed by $prJ'$ specialises to $x_n'$, the embedding $\mathrm{emb} : B \to$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` is the specialisation map of stalks along $hsp$, followed by the stalk map of $prJ'$, the stalk map of `eeta`, and the inverse of `Meta.ffEquiv`. Finally $bcA :=$ `bcMap (ΓM M H) hj ρ (residue A) rfl`. The sections $gu$, $gv$, the element $\mathrm{param}$, the open $VM$, the map $pr\sigma$ and the map $\sigma_B$ are named in the statement but do not occur in its conclusion.
--
--   Conclusion. For every $t \in B$ that is a unit there exist an open $U'$ of $X_A$, a proof that the image of $n$ in $X_A$ along `pullback.fst` followed by `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` followed by $bcA$ lies in $U'$, a proof that the generic point of `Meta.C` lies in $\mathtt{eeta}^{-1}(prA^{-1}(U'))$, and a section $\gamma \in \Gamma(X_A, U')$ such that: $\gamma$ is a unit of that ring, and the image of $\gamma$ under restriction along $prA$, then along `eeta`, then the germ at the generic point of `Meta.C`, followed by the inverse of `Meta.ffEquiv`, equals $\mathrm{emb}\, t$.
--
--   This is the transport step which converts a unit in the local ring of the model over the second coefficient ring $O'$ at the crossing point into a unit section of the model over the valuation ring $A$ on a neighbourhood of the corresponding point, with the same image in the geometric function field of $X_H$. It feeds into [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_isUnit_and_read_eq_and_ord_placeOn_eq_zero_of_forall_ord_eq_zero_of_forall_isUnit_evalAt_of_chart_of_residue_surjective`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_isUnit_and_read_eq_and_ord_placeOn_eq_zero_of_forall_ord_eq_zero_of_forall_isUnit_evalAt_of_chart_of_residue_surjective), where such sections are used to detect vanishing of orders at places on the geometric model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XHDRModelAtP_exists_isUnit_section_read_eq_stalkRead_of_isUnit.lean

